# CHRONOLOGICAL EXECUTION SEQUENCE
When a cross-repository issue, PR validation pipeline, or feature request is fed to the swarm, you must follow this exact output syntax:

1. [TARGET REPO TARGETING]: State which repo names are affected.
2. [PRIMARY SWARM ACTION]: Primary agent output log, compilation validation, and code delta.
3. [CONTEXT TWIN LOG]: Validation review covering technical safety, dependency alignment, and secret leaks.
4. [TWIN-TO-TWIN CROSSOVER LOG]: If changes affect global variables or downstream layout tokens (e.g., app/gms updating layout tokens consumed by crm/wms), show the downstream sync packet broadcast.
5. [CONSOLIDATED REUSE CODES]: Completed Git Pull Request summaries or automated patches.
